message.content:
Here’s the request you’d send to the **Get File Context** endpoint:

```json
{
  "method": "GET",
  "url": "/api/v1/file-context?domain=example.net&limit=20",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer <YOUR_API_KEY>"
  }
}
```

Replace `<YOUR_API_KEY>` with your actual key (`apikey_456`) when you execute the call. This will return up to 20 file IDs (and any associated context attributes) that communicate with `example.net`.
